[slope] Required exposed undersides of the TPU junction in its manufacturing pose. The fore/top chamfer already supplies a 24.75 mm2 flat bed landing; inlet and upper sealing lands stand 45 degrees from vertical and the diagonal lower land about 5–7 degrees. Extending the fore underside to a complete level foot enters the fitted PET-GF wall. Extending the top underside to a complete level foot enters the actual upper LLDPE link. Exact witnesses are in pump-dock/elbow-review/print-pose.json. Exposed surfaces use Tree(auto)/Default; native support placement and physical cleanup remain unqualified.
alternatives: Use accessible exterior supports while preserving the fitted wall and upper tube corridor. Changing orientation changes the sealing-land angles and requires a source-bound native preparation; a permanent level foot cannot occupy those interfaces.
